## The reference

The chapters above describe the editor feature by feature. The *reference*
documents each Lisp procedure on its own — every command, every buffer
primitive, every core function — grouped by tier. Read `index` first for
how an entry is laid out and what the naming conventions mean. For the
language itself (evaluation, special forms, macros, modules, errors), read
`docs/spec/lisp.md`.

